    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.basics\n\n### Description\n\nSetting `config.mappings.basic` to `true` defines a `<C-Z>` keymap, which overwrites the [suspend shortcut in Neovim](https://neovim.io/doc/user/usr_21.html#21.1).\r\n\r\nIt looks like this was intentional, based on this comment: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0d598d4901561490933bd0a93ebb608c9db4190f/lua/mini/basics.lua#L588-L590\r\n\r\nI also see that keymaps provided by mini.basics can be removed, as documented here: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-basics.txt#L212-L217\r\n\r\nHowever, I believe this is a pretty integral Unix/Neovim feature that should not be overridden by default. This appears to be commonly used, as demonstrated in this recent comment thread: https://www.reddit.com/r/vim/comments/10fboc6/how_do_you_guys_run_the_code_you_write_with_vim/j4vvho7/\r\n\r\nMy hope would be for this mapping to be changed to avoid the conflict. After installing this module I was confused as to why the `CTRl+Z` functionality broke, and I imagine others have or will face the same confusion.\r\n\r\nIf you decide to keep it as is, for anyone stumbling upon this issue, the original behavior can be restored by adding `vim.keymap.del('n', '<C-z>')` after your mini.basics setup. But this seems like a hard to discover workaround, with the easiest solution being to use a different keymap.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Set `config.mappings.basic` to `true`\r\n2. Attempt to use `<C-z>` command\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNeovim is suspended (closes, takes you back to shell).\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nMini.basics tries to run a correct spelling command. You may see an error message such as `E756 spell checking is not possible` depending on your cursor position.",
